class EquivalenceDegree {
  definition {
    The degree of equivalence between a localized concept and its
    counterpart in another language, per ISO 704:2022 §7.7.3.

    Equivalence is not always full. Cross-language terminology work
    needs to distinguish:
      - full:        same concept, same intension across languages
      - partial:     overlapping but not identical intension
                     (e.g., English "privacy" vs German "Privatheit")
      - none:        no corresponding concept in this language
      - directional: monodirectional equivalence
                     (e.g., glue ↔ adhésif in Canadian French context,
                     but not the reverse — see ISO 704:2022 §7.7.3)

    Defaults to `full` when omitted. Partial and directional should
    be accompanied by an `equivalence_note` explaining the difference.
  }
  values {
    full
    partial
    none
    directional
  }
}
